  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday night through next Sunday)\nIssued at 205 PM CDT Sun Sep 6 2026\n\nOn Tuesday the ridge aloft will strengthen over the Mid-South, and \nbecome elongated east-west from the Carolinas across the southern \nPlains and into the Southwest. The high will become refocused over \nArizona/New Mexico Thursday and Friday, and then is progged to shift \nback east over Texas for the weekend. An uptick in temperatures is \nexpected in the mid-week into the weekend with some strengthening of \nthe 850mb thermal ridge. Daily highs are forecast to increase to 100-\n104 degrees across the Big Country, and an increasing part of our \ncentral counties will see triple digit highs. These forecast highs \nwill be within a few degrees of the daily record highs Wednesday \nthrough Saturday (September 9-12). \n\nBy the early part of next week the high is forecast to become re-\ncentered over the southeastern CONUS. Forecast uncertainty is \nincreased Sunday into next week regarding rain chances in our area, \nwith different depictions in the medium range models. Temperatures \nshould back off at least a few degrees by that time, but look to \nremain above normal.",
